**Source Note: M439C883E759B**

**Title:** *Geometry-orchestrated objective reduction from a multiscale resonance chain: Polyatomic time crystals*

**Authors:** Pushpendra Singh (IIT Mandi, Sapiotectronics Lab / CQST), Stuart Hameroff (Quantum Life Technologies), Anirban Bandyopadhyay (NIMS Tsukuba)

**Venue:** Chaos, Solitons & Fractals 213 (2026) 119151 · doi:10.1016/j.chaos.2026.119151 · received 2026-05-22, accepted 2026-09-04, online 2026-09-25. [p1, p19]

**Subject:** A normalized nonlinear-systems framework that recasts Orch-OR as a falsifiable geometry-controlled synchronization problem. A "polyatomic time crystal" (PTC) is defined as a finite, dissipative, multiscale ensemble of commensurate phase-locked clocks — spanning π-electron aromatic pockets, microtubules, organelle assemblies, and macroscopic body modes — whose coupling is shaped by three geometric invariants: curvature concentration (κ), host–guest nesting (η), and sectorized geometric phase (σ). The same invariants feed a normalized Diósi–Penrose self-energy proxy, yielding relative collapse-time contours overlaid on the synchronization landscape. [p1–p4]

**Genre:** Theoretical/computational physics paper; mathematical-modeling forward, with explicit falsification protocol and proposed experiments. Carefully hedged epistemics: the DP functional is a normalized proxy for *relative* comparisons, not an absolute gravitational-collapse energy. [p8, p17–p18]

**Model structure:**

- **Model I — PTC state space & resonance network.** N=120 phase oscillators grouped into low/intermediate/high frequency families with log-spaced ωᵢ. Geometry-dependent Sakaguchi–Kuramoto dynamics: dθᵢ/dt = ωᵢ(δ) + (1/N)Σⱼ Kᵢⱼ(κ,η,A)·sin[θⱼ−θᵢ−αᵢⱼ(κ,η,σ,A,δ)], where Kᵢⱼ = clip(MᵢⱼK₀·exp(−ln²(ωᵢ/ωⱼ)/2ℓ²)(1+bκκCᵢⱼ)(1+bηηHᵢⱼ)(1−b_A·A)) with binary connectivity mask Mᵢⱼ dense intra-band and sparse adjacent-band; αᵢⱼ collects α₀ + aκκ(cᵢ−cⱼ) + aηη(hᵢ−hⱼ) + aσσ·2π(sᵢ−sⱼ)/S + a_A·A·ξᵢⱼ + a_δ·δ·qᵢⱼ. Six-component geometric state space M = (L, K, F, Φ, T, H). [p3–p6]
- **Model II — OR trigger functional.** Voxelized density contrast Δρ between alternative locked configurations (Δρ_mech from curvature/nesting geometry + Δρ_field from stored EM/elastic energy u/c² in low-polarity cavities); softened-Newton-kernel self-energy E_G[I], τ̂_OR = ħ/E_G normalized to a reference. [p8, p10–p11]
- **Model III — geometry→invariants→dynamics map.** Local constitutive relations: elastic bending U_κ quadratic in curvature deviation (Helfrich-style), host–guest dielectric energy linear in η under fixed-charge boundary conditions (monotonicity explicitly scoped), sector term periodic. Finite-difference monotonicity check defines the calibrated domain. [p11–p13]
- **Probability-control surface.** Hazard model Z(G,X,t) = 1−exp[−t(λ_G·G + λ_D(1−X))] with G = normalized E_G and X = coherence-protection factor = r. Z=0.5 ridge as neutral benchmark. [p9, p13, p15]

**Key numerical results:** [p13, Table 2]

1. Discrete locking plateaus in r(κ,η) separated by bifurcation-like ridges (sparse cross-band link rearrangement).
2. τ̂_OR contours compress where curvature/nesting raise energy-density contrast; sector re-partitioning shears the contour family.
3. Anesthetic perturbation lowers steady-state r and slows approach to locking (π-pocket de-locking + band broadening).
4. Sensitivity tornado at (G,X)=(0.5,0.6): G (via E_G) is the largest lever, then time window T, λ₀; negative β sensitivity.
5. Two-parameter (A, δ) perturbation diagram: anesthetic crosses a de-locking ridge (r=0.5) whose position shifts under cavity/dielectric detuning — the headline falsifiable prediction.

**Five key predictions:** discrete ~12-decade cross-scale frequency lattice; geometry-dependent τ_OR; anesthetic-sensitive de-locking at π-rich sites; path-selective ETPA readout along helical/π-rich routes; cavity/vacuum (Casimir–Polder) tuning of sector structure. [p13–p14]

**Proposed validation (E1–E3):** E1 — electro-oriented taxol-stabilized MT films under broadband THz-TDS (0.2–3 THz) + VNA (10 MHz–40 GHz) + lock-in kHz–Hz, with microcurvature substrates, layer-by-layer spacing stacks, and isoflurane/sevoflurane titration in vapor-tight cuvettes; controls = depolymerized tubulin, BSA, inert polymers. E2 — SPDC entangled two-photon absorption vs classical 2PA at ultra-low flux, pathway-resolved amplitude proxy qᵢⱼ. E3 — nanometric cavity/dielectric spacers (nanoparticle-on-mirror) modulating local mode densities. Falsifier logic: "any two independent null results would strongly disfavor" the mechanism. [p14–p18]

**Empirical scaffolding cited:** microtubule dielectric anisotropy/electro-orientation (Minoura & Muto 2006); excitonic transport + Fano Raman lineshapes in tubulin aromatics; anesthetic-tubulin binding literature; the group's own Dodecanogram platform (12 synchronized bands, 1 Hz–5.31 GHz); MHz "triplet-of-triplet" spectral structures across proteins/cells/plants/animals/humans; propofol EEG+DDG clinical study; lidocaine organellar cascade in tomato root cells; silver-nanoparticle plasmonic scalp front-end. [p2, p6, p11]

**Striking details:**

- The PTC is explicitly *not* claimed as an equilibrium phase of matter or evidence of biological OR — it denotes a finite dissipative ensemble of commensurate clocks selected by geometry-dependent coupling. Unusually careful scope-setting for this corner of the literature. [p4]
- N=120 is a coarse-grained resonant-domain count, not tubulin dimers; finite-size robustness tested at N=50/120/250/500 with r=0.5 boundary convergence. [p6]
- Meninges claim: "only MHz frequencies can reflect from 14 layers" — the group's consciousness marker lives in MHz scalp patterns (DDG). [p11, refs 33–34]
- Curvature→collapse link: curved microtubules store more lattice energy AND break more (Tsitkov 2022), so geometry literally prices the collapse-time proxy. [p12]

